uBridge is a simple user-space bridge used by GNS3 to interconnect emulated
devices. It links network interfaces through UDP tunnels, UNIX sockets, TAP
devices and physical Ethernet interfaces, and can capture traffic with libpcap
and apply per-bridge packet filters (delay, jitter, loss, corruption).

The GNS3 server starts one uBridge hypervisor per project and talks to it over
a line-based control protocol through a UNIX socket or TCP.
